    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Bi et al. (2015) & Park et al. (2015) zero-temperature shape-index unjamming & asthmatic bronchial epithelial rigidity transition (Human (Homo sapiens) bronchial epithelial monolayer & Drosophila epithelial sheet)",
            "Bi et al. (2015) & Park et al. (2015) zero-temperature shape-index unjamming & asthmatic bronchial epithelial rigidity transition faithfully reproduces Human (Homo sapiens) bronchial epithelial monolayer & Drosophila epithelial sheet morphology" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bi-vertex-glass-jamming-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bi-vertex-glass-jamming-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bi-vertex-glass-jamming-3> ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2015-bi-vertex-glass-jamming.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Human (Homo sapiens) bronchial epithelial monolayer & Drosophila epithelial sheet specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0cb0132/2015-bi-vertex-glass-jamming.py> ;
        schema:about "Human (Homo sapiens) bronchial epithelial monolayer & Drosophila epithelial sheet" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not model 3D mucociliary beating hydrodynamics or sub-epithelial airway smooth muscle contraction.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic confluent monolayer vertex-Voronoi simulation across 4 regimes (Non-Asthmatic Solid p_0=3.70, Critical Point p_0^*=3.813, Asthmatic Fluid p_0=3.955, and Zero-Perimeter-Modulus Ablation r=0.0), 8-point p_0 phase sweep in [3.55, 4.00], and Park et al. (2015) Days 3-18 bronchial maturation trajectories.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Junction-guided Voronoi segmentation of the human in situ monolayer micrograph (`human_epithelial_monolayer_specimen.jpg`, N=101 interior cells, <q>=3.7961, k-Gamma correlation r = 0.9334).",
            "reported_in_source: Bi, Lopez, Schwarz & Manning (2015) Nature Physics Eqs. 1-2 & Figs. 1-4: dimensionless vertex energy e = (1/2) sum [(a_i - 1)^2 + r(p_i - p_0)^2] exhibits a density-independent rigidity transition at critical target shape index p_0^* approx 3.813 (> p_5 approx 3.8119 > p_hex approx 3.7224), where T1 energy barrier Delta e_T1(p_0) and static shear modulus G(p_0) vanish identically for p_0 >= p_0^*.",
            "reported_in_source: Park et al. (2015) Nature Materials Figs. 1-4 & Atia et al. (2018) Nature Physics Figs. 1-2: primary human bronchial epithelial cells (HBECs) from non-asthmatic donors jam into a solid monolayer by Day 14 (q = 3.792 < 3.813), whereas asthmatic donor HBECs (q = 3.955 > 3.813) and mechanically compressed HBECs (30 cm H2O, q = 3.945 > 3.813) remain unjammed, with standardized cell shapes obeying a universal k-Gamma distribution.",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D apical polygonal projection of pseudostratified bronchial and simple monolayer epithelia." ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0cb0132/2015-bi-vertex-glass-jamming.py; output: docs/media/vertex_glass_jamming_comparison.png; organism: Human (Homo sapiens) bronchial epithelial monolayer & Drosophila epithelial sheet; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/0cb0132; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 52abc2dcaa2857a7c9b54a7d8ac8d7ebb1e0481dc0dc957ca72fa6bc9190d466; artifact_sha256: 6b4fc774e8883b673018abcacc3e2f6d0542ce1dcba17f0f1c75210d9cc7c224; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Bi, Lopez, Schwarz & Manning (2015) Nature Physics Eqs. 1-2 & Figs. 1-4: dimensionless vertex energy e = (1/2) sum [(a_i - 1)^2 + r(p_i - p_0)^2] exhibits a density-independent rigidity transition at critical target shape index p_0^* approx 3.813 (> p_5 approx 3.8119 > p_hex approx 3.7224), where T1 energy barrier Delta e_T1(p_0) and static shear modulus G(p_0) vanish identically for p_0 >= p_0^*. | Park et al. (2015) Nature Materials Figs. 1-4 & Atia et al. (2018) Nature Physics Figs. 1-2: primary human bronchial epithelial cells (HBECs) from non-asthmatic donors jam into a solid monolayer by Day 14 (q = 3.792 < 3.813), whereas asthmatic donor HBECs (q = 3.955 > 3.813) and mechanically compressed HBECs (30 cm H2O, q = 3.945 > 3.813) remain unjammed, with standardized cell shapes obeying a universal k-Gamma distribution.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic confluent monolayer vertex-Voronoi simulation across 4 regimes (Non-Asthmatic Solid p_0=3.70, Critical Point p_0^*=3.813, Asthmatic Fluid p_0=3.955, and Zero-Perimeter-Modulus Ablation r=0.0), 8-point p_0 phase sweep in [3.55, 4.00], and Park et al. (2015) Days 3-18 bronchial maturation trajectories. | Junction-guided Voronoi segmentation of the human in situ monolayer micrograph (`human_epithelial_monolayer_specimen.jpg`, N=101 interior cells, <q>=3.7961, k-Gamma correlation r = 0.9334).; transfer_boundary: 2D apical polygonal projection of pseudostratified bronchial and simple monolayer epithelia.; does_not_claim: Does not model 3D mucociliary beating hydrodynamics or sub-epithelial airway smooth muscle contraction.]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1038/nmat4357>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nphys3471>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-018-0089-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevX.6.021011>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1140/epje/i2010-10677-0> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-specimen-match> ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v2-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v2-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v2-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v2-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v2-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v2-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v2-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v2-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-8> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Zero-Temperature Shape-Index Unjamming (Bi-Manning Vertex Rigidity Transition & Asthmatic Bronchial Epithelial Jamming)" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 9.1e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Vandenberg, Adams & Levin (2012) & Pinet et al. (2019) Picasso tadpole craniofacial attractor remodeling (Xenopus laevis African clawed frog tadpole and froglet)",
            "Vandenberg, Adams & Levin (2012) & Pinet et al. (2019) Picasso tadpole craniofacial attractor remodeling faithfully reproduces Xenopus laevis African clawed frog tadpole and froglet morphology" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-3> ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2019-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Xenopus laevis African clawed frog tadpole and froglet specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 92.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2019-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap.py> ;
        schema:about "Xenopus laevis African clawed frog tadpole and froglet" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D finite-element cartilage biomechanics of Meckel's/palatoquadrate chondrocytes or explicit collagen-I fibril cleavage kinetics",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Automated PCA craniofacial axis, snout apex, 40-bin dorsal head width profile (r=0.9114), and bilateral dorsolateral eye detection (N=2 eyes, |Delta s|=0.0023) on xenopus_craniofacial_specimen.jpg",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Coupled 5-landmark Procrustes attractor ODE dx_i/dt = eta_MMP * [-K_i*(x_i - x_i^*) - sum_j C_ij*((x_i - x_j) - (x_i^* - x_j^*))] integrated via RK4 across NF stages 45->65 for 6 experimental regimes plus a 15x15 (alpha_pert, eta_MMP) morphospace grid",
            "reported_in_source: Pinet et al. (2019) Development 146:dev175893 thyroid-hormone-independent pre-metamorphic craniofacial remodeling and arrest under matrix metalloproteinase (MMP) inhibition (GM6001)",
            "reported_in_source: Proportional organ migration velocity scaling with displacement distance from target morphology (Vandenberg et al. 2012 Fig. 6) and restoration of bilateral facial symmetry",
            "reported_in_source: Vandenberg, Adams & Levin (2012) Dev. Dyn. 241:863-878 craniofacial landmark tracking of eyes, nostrils/nares, and jaws across Nieuwkoop-Faber stages 45 to 65 showing goal-directed 'Picasso tadpole' normalization to froglet anatomy vs open-loop fixed-displacement vector failure",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal Procrustes craniofacial landmark coordinates (left/right eye, left/right naris, jaw midpoint) and reconstructed froglet head contour compared against dorsal Xenopus laevis specimen geometry" ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2019-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap.py; output: docs/media/xenopus_craniofacial_remap_comparison.png; organism: Xenopus laevis African clawed frog tadpole and froglet; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: b508063893dc2ba283709bbd6f8bccfb0c0050e2d4a352a6be0037d6b7fbad04; artifact_sha256: a05e5ee5c81988c6442c768499a76a5f4e0a7ddae1b23bca3a0585f34a108cc2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/paper_citations.bib=f5f4d62c485aca75..., datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/scout_manifest.json=96534373d259eb28..., datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/xenopus_craniofacial_remap_reference.json=2656eaab51beb4ca..., datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/xenopus_craniofacial_specimen.jpg=8832f70a57f3d1c4...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Vandenberg, Adams & Levin (2012) Dev. Dyn. 241:863-878 craniofacial landmark tracking of eyes, nostrils/nares, and jaws across Nieuwkoop-Faber stages 45 to 65 showing goal-directed 'Picasso tadpole' normalization to froglet anatomy vs open-loop fixed-displacement vector failure | Proportional organ migration velocity scaling with displacement distance from target morphology (Vandenberg et al. 2012 Fig. 6) and restoration of bilateral facial symmetry | Pinet et al. (2019) Development 146:dev175893 thyroid-hormone-independent pre-metamorphic craniofacial remodeling and arrest under matrix metalloproteinase (MMP) inhibition (GM6001); reconstructed_in_script: Coupled 5-landmark Procrustes attractor ODE dx_i/dt = eta_MMP * [-K_i*(x_i - x_i^*) - sum_j C_ij*((x_i - x_j) - (x_i^* - x_j^*))] integrated via RK4 across NF stages 45->65 for 6 experimental regimes plus a 15x15 (alpha_pert, eta_MMP) morphospace grid | Automated PCA craniofacial axis, snout apex, 40-bin dorsal head width profile (r=0.9114), and bilateral dorsolateral eye detection (N=2 eyes, |Delta s|=0.0023) on xenopus_craniofacial_specimen.jpg; transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal Procrustes craniofacial landmark coordinates (left/right eye, left/right naris, jaw midpoint) and reconstructed froglet head contour compared against dorsal Xenopus laevis specimen geometry; does_not_claim: 3D finite-element cartilage biomechanics of Meckel's/palatoquadrate chondrocytes or explicit collagen-I fibril cleavage kinetics]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.23770>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2016.0555>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.073759>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.175893> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-model-fidelity>,
