    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model (Homo sapiens vs Mus musculus (hPSC-derived presomitic mesoderm / axioloid somite organoid))",
            "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model faithfully reproduces Homo sapiens vs Mus musculus (hPSC-derived presomitic mesoderm / axioloid somite organoid) morphology" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-3> ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Homo sapiens vs Mus musculus (hPSC-derived presomitic mesoderm / axioloid somite organoid) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.5/100, audit 2026-10-19-human-somite-organoid-clock-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py> ;
        schema:about "Homo sapiens vs Mus musculus (hPSC-derived presomitic mesoderm / axioloid somite organoid)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Full 3D actomyosin apical constriction mechanics during epithelial somite rosette clefting",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 6-regime genetic & metabolic perturbation series (mouse WT, mouse + hHES7 swap, human WT, human + LbNOX NAD+ rescue, human + sodium azide ETC inhibition, and intronless Hes7 subcritical collapse; Pearson r = 0.9999, RMSE = 2.18 min)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 6-species vertebrate segmentation clock allometry (r = 0.9970), human axioloid traveling-wave kymograph, and bilateral dorsal somite row DoG segmentation on human_somite_organoid_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Delayed autoinhibitory HES7 transcriptional-translational feedback loop (TTFL) RK2 DDE solver reproducing mouse WT (122.00 min), human WT (300.01 min, ratio = 2.4591), and exact tempo rescaling collapse (std = 2.32e-13 nM, linear r = 1.0000)",
            "reported_in_source: Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) Nature 580:113-118 discovery of ~5.0 h (300 min) HES7-Achilles oscillations in human pluripotent stem-cell-derived presomitic mesoderm vs ~2.0 h (122 min) in mouse PSM",
            "reported_in_source: Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2023) Nature 613:550-557 demonstration that mitochondrial electron transport chain activity and cytosolic NAD+/NADH ratio modulate global translation rate and segmentation clock period (LbNOX acceleration vs sodium azide/rotenone slowdown)",
            "reported_in_source: Matsuda et al. (2020) Science 369:1450-1455 demonstration that species-specific HES7 intron splicing delay (tau_tx) and protein/mRNA half-lives (t_1/2), rather than the hHES7 genomic locus sequence alone, govern the 2.5x human clock slowdown",
            "transfer_boundary: Single-cell and 1D/2D axioloid HES7 DDE kinetics compared with dorsal vertebrate paraxial somite SEM metameric periodicity" ;
