    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model & Lewis's law epithelial packing (Fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster) 3rd-instar larval wing imaginal disc & pupal wing epithelium)",
            "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model & Lewis's law epithelial packing faithfully reproduces Fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster) 3rd-instar larval wing imaginal disc & pupal wing epithelium morphology" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-3> ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster) 3rd-instar larval wing imaginal disc & pupal wing epithelium specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/b9976f8/2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py> ;
        schema:about "Fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster) 3rd-instar larval wing imaginal disc & pupal wing epithelium" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not model basal extracellular matrix curvature or 3D apico-basal scutoid transitions.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic apical vertex packing and mitotic cleavage simulation across 4 mechanical regimes (Proliferating Wing Disc, Post-Mitotic Pupal Wing, High-Contractility Case I, and Soft Case II), 2D (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar) phase diagram, UV laser junction ablation recoil curves, and 7-point continuous Lambda_bar sweep.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Junction-guided Voronoi-watershed segmentation of the apical junction-stained polygonal epithelial micrograph (`drosophila_wing_epithelium_specimen.jpg`, N=37 interior cells, P(6)=0.4865, P(n) correlation r = 0.9913).",
            "reported_in_source: Farhadifar et al. (2007) Fig. 3-4, Gibson et al. (2006) Nature & Classen et al. (2005) Dev. Cell: proliferating 3rd-instar Drosophila wing disc exhibits P(6) approx 0.455 (mu_2 = 0.765) and obeys Lewis's Law <A_n>/<A> = (n-2)/4, whereas post-mitotic pupal wing annealing increases P(6) to ~0.78 (mu_2 = 0.250).",
            "reported_in_source: Farhadifar, Röper, Aigouy, Eaton & Jülicher (2007) Current Biology Eqs. 1-2 & Fig. 2A: apical epithelial vertex energy functional E({r_i}) = sum (K/2)(A_alpha - A^(0))^2 + sum Lambda_{ij} l_{ij} + sum (Gamma/2) L_alpha^2 parameterized by (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar), partitioning ground states into Case I (rigid hexagonal, canonical wing disc Lambda_bar=0.12, Gamma_bar=0.04), Case II (soft network), and Case III (cell collapse).",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D apical junctional projection of 3D pseudostratified/columnar wing imaginal disc epithelial cells." ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/b9976f8/2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_wing_vertex_model_comparison.png; organism: Fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster) 3rd-instar larval wing imaginal disc & pupal wing epithelium; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/b9976f8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 00f70e92aaa338b22956554153bb93fbccd372cdaae2e3f47f4744bcadfffe52; artifact_sha256: d1c94b16e8a8dabd2fa188b59f66091e4dd352b73f3ec1401c0579b6e896bbf1; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Farhadifar, Röper, Aigouy, Eaton & Jülicher (2007) Current Biology Eqs. 1-2 & Fig. 2A: apical epithelial vertex energy functional E({r_i}) = sum (K/2)(A_alpha - A^(0))^2 + sum Lambda_{ij} l_{ij} + sum (Gamma/2) L_alpha^2 parameterized by (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar), partitioning ground states into Case I (rigid hexagonal, canonical wing disc Lambda_bar=0.12, Gamma_bar=0.04), Case II (soft network), and Case III (cell collapse). | Farhadifar et al. (2007) Fig. 3-4, Gibson et al. (2006) Nature & Classen et al. (2005) Dev. Cell: proliferating 3rd-instar Drosophila wing disc exhibits P(6) approx 0.455 (mu_2 = 0.765) and obeys Lewis's Law <A_n>/<A> = (n-2)/4, whereas post-mitotic pupal wing annealing increases P(6) to ~0.78 (mu_2 = 0.250).; reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic apical vertex packing and mitotic cleavage simulation across 4 mechanical regimes (Proliferating Wing Disc, Post-Mitotic Pupal Wing, High-Contractility Case I, and Soft Case II), 2D (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar) phase diagram, UV laser junction ablation recoil curves, and 7-point continuous Lambda_bar sweep. | Junction-guided Voronoi-watershed segmentation of the apical junction-stained polygonal epithelial micrograph (`drosophila_wing_epithelium_specimen.jpg`, N=37 interior cells, P(6)=0.4865, P(n) correlation r = 0.9913).; transfer_boundary: 2D apical junctional projection of 3D pseudostratified/columnar wing imaginal disc epithelial cells.; does_not_claim: Does not model basal extracellular matrix curvature or 3D apico-basal scutoid transitions.]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.1090380305>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.11.049>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2005.10.016>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature05014>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1080/13642810108205772> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-model-fidelity>,
