    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law (Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation))",
            "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law faithfully reproduces Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation) morphology" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-3> ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py, docs/media/runions_leaf_venation_growth.gif, runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.3/100, audit 2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/docs/media/runions_leaf_venation_growth.gif>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv> ;
        schema:about "Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 2D planar lamina space-colonization and pipe-model radius propagation do not model 3D mesophyll thickness or stomatal transpiration dynamics",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba (Table 1 Fig. 10) and closed dicot (Table 1 Fig. 15) space-colonization simulators with persistent V(s) source tagging and planar segment-intersection checks, multiscale Horton-Strahler vascular tree measurement, and planar dual areole loop nesting on both simulated networks and segmented specimen photographs",
            "reported_in_source: Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph",
            "reported_in_source: Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01)",
            "reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with persistent tagged-source anastomosis",
            "transfer_boundary: Direct comparison of simulated planar dual areole nesting and Strahler bifurcation scaling against segmented leaf skeleton specimens and Price et al. (2013) / Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) empirical benchmarks" ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/docs/media/runions_leaf_venation_growth.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv; output: runions_leaf_venation_comparison.png; organism: Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/c89d18d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 9c51f0ee1bb18dac15303bbc28f21b848e721403f4cfc6f6459cd6e7325c2ab9; artifact_sha256: d7f0922fe27597dd1757a5525cd01c5a03356d817ba67aec405a918bfb794e34; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/venation/ginkgo_open_venation_specimen.jpg=5a620943881fe698..., datasets/venation/reticulate_vein_skeleton_specimen.jpg=6d06d3e545bd585b..., datasets/venation/venation_reference.json=c22c5f4e26f3e2c6...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-18-venation-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with persistent tagged-source anastomosis | Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01) | Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph; reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba (Table 1 Fig. 10) and closed dicot (Table 1 Fig. 15) space-colonization simulators with persistent V(s) source tagging and planar segment-intersection checks, multiscale Horton-Strahler vascular tree measurement, and planar dual areole loop nesting on both simulated networks and segmented specimen photographs; transfer_boundary: Direct comparison of simulated planar dual areole nesting and Strahler bifurcation scaling against segmented leaf skeleton specimens and Price et al. (2013) / Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) empirical benchmarks; does_not_claim: 2D planar lamina space-colonization and pipe-model radius propagation do not model 3D mesophyll thickness or stomatal transpiration dynamics]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004680>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0037994>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0085420> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-specimen-match> ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-7> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Auxin Space-Colonization, Murray's Minimum-Work Vascular Law & Planar Dual Loop Nesting" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 9.13e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing and Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling (Arabidopsis thaliana (cotyledon & leaf epidermal pavement cells))",
            "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing and Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling faithfully reproduces Arabidopsis thaliana (cotyledon & leaf epidermal pavement cells) morphology" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-3> ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Arabidopsis thaliana (cotyledon & leaf epidermal pavement cells) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 93.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-pavement-cell-lobing-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py> ;
        schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana (cotyledon & leaf epidermal pavement cells)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Full 3D finite-element shell modeling of dome deflection z(x,y) coupled to discrete microtubule filament polymerization stochastics",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 196-node periodic anticlinal boundary coupled ROP2-RIC4 / ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 reaction-diffusion PDE integrator reproducing intracortical mutual exclusion (r = -0.9899), trans-wall lobe-neck complementarity (r = 0.9998), 24.5 um lobe wavelength, and exact intercellular area conservation",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Automated DoG + zero-compactness watershed segmentation of 10 interlocking puzzle-shaped pavement cells from the SHA-256-locked Arabidopsis thaliana leaf epidermis SEM micrograph (`arabidopsis_pavement_cell_specimen.jpg`, mean S = 0.720, min S = 0.626, mean L = 1.506)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Exact 2D Euclidean Distance Transform Largest Empty Circle (R_LEC) and ConvexHull solidity/lobeyness solver across cell area growth A in [250, 4500] um^2 for wild-type Col-0 puzzle cells, unlobed isotropic cells, ktn1/ric1 and rop2 rop4 mutants, and parallel-file monocot epidermis",
            "reported_in_source: Fu et al. (2005) Cell 120:687-700 & Lin et al. (2013) Curr Biol 23:290-297 antagonistic cortical ROP2-RIC4 (actin lobe outgrowth) and ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 (katanin-mediated microtubule neck bundling) polarization in antiphase across shared anticlinal cell walls, and lobeyness collapse in rop2 rop4 RNAi and ktn1/ric1 mutants",
            "reported_in_source: Sapala et al. (2018) eLife 7:e32794 outer periclinal cell wall tensile stress scaling with Largest Empty Circle radius (sigma_max ~ P * R_LEC / h), demonstrating that interdigitated puzzle lobing pins R_LEC near ~11.4 um as cell area expands to 4500 um^2 whereas isotropic polygonal/mutant cells grow as sqrt(A/pi)",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D anticlinal boundary PDE and spring-remodeled polygonal contours with Euclidean Distance Transform R_LEC mapped to 2D epidermal SEM projections" ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py; output: docs/media/pavement_cell_lobing_comparison.png; organism: Arabidopsis thaliana (cotyledon & leaf epidermal pavement cells); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 972460a5749d7d30868f5de9c61bcfd278fa143f89d629090a75b7aa4ebdc287; artifact_sha256: 8df82fae6327068a70bf77aefe4e8d85e05dc9e0d53c002655ab4d6165803e01; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/arabidopsis_pavement_cell_specimen.jpg=4b7c1062f6ebfd6e..., datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/paper_citations.bib=e5d0ea8ec26365c9..., datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/pavement_cell_lobing_reference.json=de4e6daab5eae4a0..., datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/scout_manifest.json=72c917ec10ac1a55...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-pavement-cell-lobing-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Sapala et al. (2018) eLife 7:e32794 outer periclinal cell wall tensile stress scaling with Largest Empty Circle radius (sigma_max ~ P * R_LEC / h), demonstrating that interdigitated puzzle lobing pins R_LEC near ~11.4 um as cell area expands to 4500 um^2 whereas isotropic polygonal/mutant cells grow as sqrt(A/pi) | Fu et al. (2005) Cell 120:687-700 & Lin et al. (2013) Curr Biol 23:290-297 antagonistic cortical ROP2-RIC4 (actin lobe outgrowth) and ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 (katanin-mediated microtubule neck bundling) polarization in antiphase across shared anticlinal cell walls, and lobeyness collapse in rop2 rop4 RNAi and ktn1/ric1 mutants; reconstructed_in_script: Exact 2D Euclidean Distance Transform Largest Empty Circle (R_LEC) and ConvexHull solidity/lobeyness solver across cell area growth A in [250, 4500] um^2 for wild-type Col-0 puzzle cells, unlobed isotropic cells, ktn1/ric1 and rop2 rop4 mutants, and parallel-file monocot epidermis | 196-node periodic anticlinal boundary coupled ROP2-RIC4 / ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 reaction-diffusion PDE integrator reproducing intracortical mutual exclusion (r = -0.9899), trans-wall lobe-neck complementarity (r = 0.9998), 24.5 um lobe wavelength, and exact intercellular area conservation | Automated DoG + zero-compactness watershed segmentation of 10 interlocking puzzle-shaped pavement cells from the SHA-256-locked Arabidopsis thaliana leaf epidermis SEM micrograph (`arabidopsis_pavement_cell_specimen.jpg`, mean S = 0.720, min S = 0.626, mean L = 1.506); transfer_boundary: 2D anticlinal boundary PDE and spring-remodeled polygonal contours with Euclidean Distance Transform R_LEC mapped to 2D epidermal SEM projections; does_not_claim: Full 3D finite-element shell modeling of dome deflection z(x,y) coupled to discrete microtubule filament polymerization stochastics]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2004.12.026>,
