    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation (Danio rerio (zebrafish tailbud mesodermal progenitor zone MPZ & presomitic mesoderm PSM))",
            "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation faithfully reproduces Danio rerio (zebrafish tailbud mesodermal progenitor zone MPZ & presomitic mesoderm PSM) morphology" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-3> ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio rerio (zebrafish tailbud mesodermal progenitor zone MPZ & presomitic mesoderm PSM) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.4/100, audit 2026-10-19-neuromesodermal-jamming-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0cb0132/2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py> ;
        schema:about "Danio rerio (zebrafish tailbud mesodermal progenitor zone MPZ & presomitic mesoderm PSM)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not model 3D notochord vacuolation turgor mechanics or anterior somite epithelialization clefting.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Continuous posterior-to-anterior active-foam & Bingham viscoplastic solver across x in [0, 300] um (`solve_ap_jamming_profile`, r_sigma_y = 0.9989, r_kT1 = 0.9922, jamming crossover x* = 81.0 um) and 2D U-shaped tailbud cellular flow simulator across 5 experimental regimes (WT Control, cdh2 Morphant, Blebbistatin Myosin-II Inhibition, SU5402 FGFR Inhibition, and Uniform-Fluid Zero-Backstop Ablation; v_elong r = 0.9717, L-R asymmetry r = 0.9851).",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Nuclear-seeded Voronoi tessellation and regional interstitial space segmentation of the Danio rerio posterior tailbud lightsheet micrograph (`zebrafish_tailbud_psm_specimen.jpg`, IDR0051, N = 391 nuclei, <z> = 5.88, AP compaction r = 0.9915).",
            "reported_in_source: Kim et al. (2021) Nature Physics 17:859-866 & Mongera et al. (2018) Fig. 4: active tension fluctuations fluidize the MPZ (sigma_A > sigma_y) via frequent T1 neighbor exchanges, whereas the jammed solid A-PSM (sigma_y >> sigma_A) serves as an internal mechanical backstop that rectifies MPZ progenitor addition into unidirectional posterior elongation and preserves left-right symmetry; N-cadherin (cdh2) knockdown expands phi_ECS > 14%, unjamming the PSM, slowing elongation, and inducing bilateral body-axis asymmetry.",
            "reported_in_source: Mongera et al. (2018) Nature 561:401-405 Figs. 1-4: along the posterior-to-anterior axis of the zebrafish tailbud, extracellular space fraction phi_ECS(x) decreases from ~14.5% in the posterior Mesodermal Progenitor Zone (MPZ) to ~4.9% in the Anterior Presomitic Mesoderm (A-PSM), driving cell packing phi_pack = 1 - phi_ECS across the rigidity-percolation threshold phi_c approx 0.860 and elevating ferrofluid-measured yield stress sigma_y(x) from ~11 Pa to ~118 Pa while active Myosin-II tension fluctuations sigma_A(x) decline from ~50 Pa to ~13 Pa.",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal-ventral optical-plane projection of the 3D U-shaped zebrafish posterior tailbud and paraxial presomitic mesoderm." ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0cb0132/2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py; output: docs/media/neuromesodermal_jamming_comparison.png; organism: Danio rerio (zebrafish tailbud mesodermal progenitor zone MPZ & presomitic mesoderm PSM); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/0cb0132; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 5225f2c29acda8d1ee81d082219556f85a1159006d552c629f56ce7d8a842027; artifact_sha256: de989cdbda2538b3ac78b567588057367c51e4f73aa8cca93a923398e4b1e838; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-neuromesodermal-jamming-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Mongera et al. (2018) Nature 561:401-405 Figs. 1-4: along the posterior-to-anterior axis of the zebrafish tailbud, extracellular space fraction phi_ECS(x) decreases from ~14.5% in the posterior Mesodermal Progenitor Zone (MPZ) to ~4.9% in the Anterior Presomitic Mesoderm (A-PSM), driving cell packing phi_pack = 1 - phi_ECS across the rigidity-percolation threshold phi_c approx 0.860 and elevating ferrofluid-measured yield stress sigma_y(x) from ~11 Pa to ~118 Pa while active Myosin-II tension fluctuations sigma_A(x) decline from ~50 Pa to ~13 Pa. | Kim et al. (2021) Nature Physics 17:859-866 & Mongera et al. (2018) Fig. 4: active tension fluctuations fluidize the MPZ (sigma_A > sigma_y) via frequent T1 neighbor exchanges, whereas the jammed solid A-PSM (sigma_y >> sigma_A) serves as an internal mechanical backstop that rectifies MPZ progenitor addition into unidirectional posterior elongation and preserves left-right symmetry; N-cadherin (cdh2) knockdown expands phi_ECS > 14%, unjamming the PSM, slowing elongation, and inducing bilateral body-axis asymmetry.; reconstructed_in_script: Continuous posterior-to-anterior active-foam & Bingham viscoplastic solver across x in [0, 300] um (`solve_ap_jamming_profile`, r_sigma_y = 0.9989, r_kT1 = 0.9922, jamming crossover x* = 81.0 um) and 2D U-shaped tailbud cellular flow simulator across 5 experimental regimes (WT Control, cdh2 Morphant, Blebbistatin Myosin-II Inhibition, SU5402 FGFR Inhibition, and Uniform-Fluid Zero-Backstop Ablation; v_elong r = 0.9717, L-R asymmetry r = 0.9851). | Nuclear-seeded Voronoi tessellation and regional interstitial space segmentation of the Danio rerio posterior tailbud lightsheet micrograph (`zebrafish_tailbud_psm_specimen.jpg`, IDR0051, N = 391 nuclei, <z> = 5.88, AP compaction r = 0.9915).; transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal-ventral optical-plane projection of the 3D U-shaped zebrafish posterior tailbud and paraxial presomitic mesoderm.; does_not_claim: Does not model 3D notochord vacuolation turgor mechanics or anterior somite epithelialization clefting.]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2013.05.052>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nmeth.4101>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-021-01215-1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-018-0479-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.090381> ;
