    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, and Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off (Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold))",
            "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, and Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off faithfully reproduces Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold) morphology" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tero-physarum-transport-network-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tero-physarum-transport-network-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tero-physarum-transport-network-3> ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 93.4/100, audit 2026-10-19-physarum-transport-network-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py> ;
        schema:about "Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D actomyosin cortex viscoelastic peristaltic calcium wave mechanics at single-filament molecular resolution",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 8-point gamma phase transition sweep in [0.8, 2.4] reproducing Tero et al. (2010) Fig. 3/4 normalized Total Length TL_MST (Pearson r = 0.99885, RMSE = 0.0363, p = 3.83e-9) and Fault Tolerance FT (Pearson r = 0.99745, RMSE = 0.0245, p = 4.12e-8), matching the Tokyo rail network at gamma = 1.8 (TL_MST = 1.7310 vs ref 1.7500, FT = 0.8089 vs ref 0.8400)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of `physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg` extracting 33 enclosed anastomosing loops (Betti-1 = 33), 3-tier vein-width hierarchy (51.96% primary trunks, 36.44% secondary, 11.59% tertiary), and degree-3 Y-junction Murray cubic ratio 0.8926 +- 0.2774 (N = 17 junctions)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Full graph Laplacian Kirchhoff pressure solver (`solve_kirchhoff_potentials`) across N_f = 36 Kanto food sources verifying nodal current conservation (error 3.57e-14 < 1e-11) and edge flux antisymmetry (error < 1e-14)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Two-path competition sweep verifying coexistence at gamma = 0.6 (Q1/I0 = 0.7322), shortest-path selection at gamma = 1.0 and 1.8 (Q1/I0 = 1.0000), gamma = 0.0 ablation control (Q1/I0 = 0.6667, delta = +0.3333), and Murray's cube law (r_1^3 + r_2^3)/r_0^3 = 1.0000 (RMSE = 3.88e-9) at gamma = 4/3",
            "reported_in_source: Multi-source Kanto / Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off across gamma in [0.8, 2.4] optimizing normalized Total Length (TL_MST ~ 1.75), Transport Efficiency (MD_MST ~ 0.85), and Fault Tolerance (FT ~ 0.84) at gamma = 1.8, plus Murray's cube law (r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3) at gamma = 4/3",
            "reported_in_source: Tero et al. (2010) Science 327:439-442 & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. 244:553-564 Hagen-Poiseuille Kirchhoff flow sum_j (D_ij/L_ij)*(p_i - p_j) = S_i coupled to nonlinear shear-stress tube adaptation dD_ij/dt = f(|Q_ij|) - mu*D_ij",
            "reported_in_source: Two-path parallel competition (L_1 < L_2) exhibiting parallel loop coexistence for gamma < 1, critical shortest-path selection at gamma_c = 1, and winner-takes-all Steiner minimum tree convergence for gamma > 1",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D planar multi-source Kirchhoff Poiseuille network and EDT medial-axis skeletonization mapped to macroscopic Physarum polycephalum plasmodial veins" ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py; output: docs/media/physarum_transport_network_comparison.png; organism: Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: a9da85cd52fbe6dcd220e87644d7d896769c3e1c0c8e71bb4976e6e20700a480; artifact_sha256: b45525865419bc46f314e54bd2198c3dd518ae47ce782756c76aa54945ad0462; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/physarum_transport_network/paper_citations.bib=95f4eb8510791507..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg=86a37f7c73c8527b..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_transport_network_reference.json=4a54186a148929f7..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/scout_manifest.json=edb27b0addb825b3...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-physarum-transport-network-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Tero et al. (2010) Science 327:439-442 & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. 244:553-564 Hagen-Poiseuille Kirchhoff flow sum_j (D_ij/L_ij)*(p_i - p_j) = S_i coupled to nonlinear shear-stress tube adaptation dD_ij/dt = f(|Q_ij|) - mu*D_ij | Two-path parallel competition (L_1 < L_2) exhibiting parallel loop coexistence for gamma < 1, critical shortest-path selection at gamma_c = 1, and winner-takes-all Steiner minimum tree convergence for gamma > 1 | Multi-source Kanto / Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off across gamma in [0.8, 2.4] optimizing normalized Total Length (TL_MST ~ 1.75), Transport Efficiency (MD_MST ~ 0.85), and Fault Tolerance (FT ~ 0.84) at gamma = 1.8, plus Murray's cube law (r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3) at gamma = 4/3; reconstructed_in_script: Full graph Laplacian Kirchhoff pressure solver (`solve_kirchhoff_potentials`) across N_f = 36 Kanto food sources verifying nodal current conservation (error 3.57e-14 < 1e-11) and edge flux antisymmetry (error < 1e-14) | 8-point gamma phase transition sweep in [0.8, 2.4] reproducing Tero et al. (2010) Fig. 3/4 normalized Total Length TL_MST (Pearson r = 0.99885, RMSE = 0.0363, p = 3.83e-9) and Fault Tolerance FT (Pearson r = 0.99745, RMSE = 0.0245, p = 4.12e-8), matching the Tokyo rail network at gamma = 1.8 (TL_MST = 1.7310 vs ref 1.7500, FT = 0.8089 vs ref 0.8400) | Two-path competition sweep verifying coexistence at gamma = 0.6 (Q1/I0 = 0.7322), shortest-path selection at gamma = 1.0 and 1.8 (Q1/I0 = 1.0000), gamma = 0.0 ablation control (Q1/I0 = 0.6667, delta = +0.3333), and Murray's cube law (r_1^3 + r_2^3)/r_0^3 = 1.0000 (RMSE = 3.88e-9) at gamma = 4/3 | Computer-vision segmentation of `physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg` extracting 33 enclosed anastomosing loops (Betti-1 = 33), 3-tier vein-width hierarchy (51.96% primary trunks, 36.44% secondary, 11.59% tertiary), and degree-3 Y-junction Murray cubic ratio 0.8926 +- 0.2774 (N = 17 junctions); transfer_boundary: 2D planar multi-source Kirchhoff Poiseuille network and EDT medial-axis skeletonization mapped to macroscopic Physarum polycephalum plasmodial veins; does_not_claim: 3D actomyosin cortex viscoelastic peristaltic calcium wave mechanics at single-filament molecular resolution]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.07.015>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.06.017>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/35035159>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1177894> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-code-traceability>,
