    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Zajac, Jones & Glazier (2000, 2003) / Bertet, Sulak & Lecuit (2004) anisotropic differential adhesion and polarized T1 junctional intercalation in convergent extension (Xenopus laevis (chordamesoderm Keller explant) & Drosophila melanogaster (germband extension epithelium))",
            "Zajac, Jones & Glazier (2000, 2003) / Bertet, Sulak & Lecuit (2004) anisotropic differential adhesion and polarized T1 junctional intercalation in convergent extension faithfully reproduces Xenopus laevis (chordamesoderm Keller explant) & Drosophila melanogaster (germband extension epithelium) morphology" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation-3> ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2003-zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Xenopus laevis (chordamesoderm Keller explant) & Drosophila melanogaster (germband extension epithelium) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.9/100, audit 2026-10-19-convergent-extension-intercalation-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2003-zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation.py> ;
        schema:about "Xenopus laevis (chordamesoderm Keller explant) & Drosophila melanogaster (germband extension epithelium)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Full 3D multicellular rosette (5+ cell vertex) resolution or explicit subcellular F-actin/EB3 microtubule polymerization reaction-diffusion kinetics",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 5-regime genetic & mechanical perturbation simulator (Wild-Type R_CE=3.859, T1/cell=1.45; Moderate Anisotropy R_CE=2.375; Xdd1/PCP mutant R_CE=1.566; Myosin II zip/sqh mutant R_CE=1.204; Isotropic Null Control R_CE=1.000, T1/cell=0.00; Pearson r=1.0000, RMSE=0.0042)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 64-cell planar-polarized T1 intercalation lattice solver with exact incompressible 2D tissue area conservation (L_AP * L_ML = A_0, error < 1e-15) and midpoint RK2 ODE convergence verification (L2 relative error 1.19e-7)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Automated confocal Xenopus explant segmentation and rose-diagram angular correlation on convergent_extension_axis_specimen.jpg (chordamesoderm L/W=4.945 vs animal cap 0.962; nematic S_2=0.613 vs 0.094; rose angular correlation r=0.9677)",
            "reported_in_source: Bertet, Sulak & Lecuit (2004) Nature 429:667-671 planar-polarized Myosin II enrichment on vertical/AP-facing type-1 junctions driving irreversible 4-way T1 vertex resolution into horizontal/ML type-3 junctions",
            "reported_in_source: Zajac, Jones & Glazier (2000, 2003) Phys. Rev. Lett. 85:2022 / J. Theor. Biol. 222:247-259 anisotropic differential adhesion energy J(theta) = J_0 - Delta_J cos(2*theta) and pure-shear convergent-extension aspect ratio scaling R_CE(t) = R_0 exp(2*dot_epsilon_T1*t)",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D planar 64-cell intercalating tissue sheet and 4-cell T1 quartet junction mechanics mapped to Xenopus chordamesoderm explants and Drosophila germband extension" ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2003-zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation.py; output: docs/media/convergent_extension_intercalation_comparison.png; organism: Xenopus laevis (chordamesoderm Keller explant) & Drosophila melanogaster (germband extension epithelium); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 70c0d2a81cec84a4a194e326ee3833640573b76865ed3d8f4c5ff14fdbf4448d; artifact_sha256: b0a09bba189a3e24e1c50bba4f1328917e09f847c0548cefb8da60430e7154e0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/convergent_extension_intercalation/convergent_extension_axis_specimen.jpg=0c2620bce19ad4cf..., datasets/convergent_extension_intercalation/convergent_extension_intercalation_reference.json=5e3d70d1a6711a38..., datasets/convergent_extension_intercalation/scout_manifest.json=66a1e6f4d0f0a745...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-convergent-extension-intercalation-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Zajac, Jones & Glazier (2000, 2003) Phys. Rev. Lett. 85:2022 / J. Theor. Biol. 222:247-259 anisotropic differential adhesion energy J(theta) = J_0 - Delta_J cos(2*theta) and pure-shear convergent-extension aspect ratio scaling R_CE(t) = R_0 exp(2*dot_epsilon_T1*t) | Bertet, Sulak & Lecuit (2004) Nature 429:667-671 planar-polarized Myosin II enrichment on vertical/AP-facing type-1 junctions driving irreversible 4-way T1 vertex resolution into horizontal/ML type-3 junctions; reconstructed_in_script: 64-cell planar-polarized T1 intercalation lattice solver with exact incompressible 2D tissue area conservation (L_AP * L_ML = A_0, error < 1e-15) and midpoint RK2 ODE convergence verification (L2 relative error 1.19e-7) | 5-regime genetic & mechanical perturbation simulator (Wild-Type R_CE=3.859, T1/cell=1.45; Moderate Anisotropy R_CE=2.375; Xdd1/PCP mutant R_CE=1.566; Myosin II zip/sqh mutant R_CE=1.204; Isotropic Null Control R_CE=1.000, T1/cell=0.00; Pearson r=1.0000, RMSE=0.0042) | Automated confocal Xenopus explant segmentation and rose-diagram angular correlation on convergent_extension_axis_specimen.jpg (chordamesoderm L/W=4.945 vs animal cap 0.962; nematic S_2=0.613 vs 0.094; rose angular correlation r=0.9677); transfer_boundary: 2D planar 64-cell intercalating tissue sheet and 4-cell T1 quartet junction mechanics mapped to Xenopus chordamesoderm explants and Drosophila germband extension; does_not_claim: Full 3D multicellular rosette (5+ cell vertex) resolution or explicit subcellular F-actin/EB3 microtubule polymerization reaction-diffusion kinetics]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(03)00033-X>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/35011077>,
