    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bi et al. (2015) & Park et al. (2015) zero-temperature shape-index unjamming & asthmatic bronchial epithelial rigidity transition — MorphoEval overall 91.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2015-bi-vertex-glass-jamming.py` (90.9/100, up from 57.3/100 in Pass 1; +33.6 points). The remediated script implements the full Bi et al. (2015) dimensionless vertex energy functional, evaluates T1 energy barrier `Delta e_T1(p_0)` and static shear modulus `G(p_0)` scaling across the critical threshold `p_0^* = 3.813`, simulates 4 distinct mechanical regimes (solid jammed `p_0=3.70, <q>=3.7756`, critical `p_0=3.813`, asthmatic fluid `p_0=3.955, <q>=3.9362`, and `r=0.0` ablation control), executes an 8-point continuous `p_0` sweep (`r = 0.9646`), models the Park et al. (2015) bronchial maturation timecourse (`r = 0.9962`), segments `N=101` cells from the SHA-256-locked human monolayer micrograph (`<q> = 3.7961`, Atia et al. 2018 `k`-Gamma `r = 0.9334`), and is backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_045_vertex_glass_jamming.lean`. Overall 91.0/100 (faithfulness 90.4, reproducibility 92.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0cb0132; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/vertex_glass_jamming_comparison.png: rendered output of 2015-bi-vertex-glass-jamming.py at 0cb0132, image/png, 1374692 B, 3075×1290 px, artifact_sha256 6b4fc774e8883b673018abcacc3e2f6d0542ce1dcba17f0f1c75210d9cc7c224 (sha256 6b4fc774e8883b673018abcacc3e2f6d0542ce1dcba17f0f1c75210d9cc7c224), spec_fingerprint 52abc2dcaa2857a7c9b54a7d8ac8d7ebb1e0481dc0dc957ca72fa6bc9190d466. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 52abc2dcaa2857a7c9b54a7d8ac8d7ebb1e0481dc0dc957ca72fa6bc9190d466; artifact_sha256: 6b4fc774e8883b673018abcacc3e2f6d0542ce1dcba17f0f1c75210d9cc7c224. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bi, Lopez, Schwarz & Manning (2015) Nature Physics Eqs. 1-2 & Figs. 1-4: dimensionless vertex energy e = (1/2) sum [(a_i - 1)^2 + r(p_i - p_0)^2] exhibits a density-independent rigidity transition at critical target shape index p_0^* approx 3.813 (> p_5 approx 3.8119 > p_hex approx 3.7224), where T1 energy barrier Delta e_T1(p_0) and static shear modulus G(p_0) vanish identically for p_0 >= p_0^*. | Park et al. (2015) Nature Materials Figs. 1-4 & Atia et al. (2018) Nature Physics Figs. 1-2: primary human bronchial epithelial cells (HBECs) from non-asthmatic donors jam into a solid monolayer by Day 14 (q = 3.792 < 3.813), whereas asthmatic donor HBECs (q = 3.955 > 3.813) and mechanically compressed HBECs (30 cm H2O, q = 3.945 > 3.813) remain unjammed, with standardized cell shapes obeying a universal k-Gamma distribution.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic confluent monolayer vertex-Voronoi simulation across 4 regimes (Non-Asthmatic Solid p_0=3.70, Critical Point p_0^*=3.813, Asthmatic Fluid p_0=3.955, and Zero-Perimeter-Modulus Ablation r=0.0), 8-point p_0 phase sweep in [3.55, 4.00], and Park et al. (2015) Days 3-18 bronchial maturation trajectories. | Junction-guided Voronoi segmentation of the human in situ monolayer micrograph (`human_epithelial_monolayer_specimen.jpg`, N=101 interior cells, <q>=3.7961, k-Gamma correlation r = 0.9334).; transfer_boundary: 2D apical polygonal projection of pseudostratified bronchial and simple monolayer epithelia.; does_not_claim: Does not model 3D mucociliary beating hydrodynamics or sub-epithelial airway smooth muscle contraction.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the zero-temperature vertex energy to self-propelled active Brownian motility forces (v_0, D_r) as in Bi et al. (2016) Physical Review X 6:021011 to map the 3D (p_0, v_0, D_r) glass transition surface." ;
        pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

