    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Code-to-model traceability: 60/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The revision substantially improves internal traceability: model constants are centralized and disclaimed as local, f2 and f3 have one mapping each, fitting and held-out roles are explicit, every-sample parity is correctly scoped, and panel D admits its illustrative time rescaling. The phenotype number can be reconstructed from Planform geometry and renderer conventions. It is not, however, a source-derived biological criterion: the 100-unit pharynx length is a renderer constant, the denominator uses padded plotting bounds, and no paper supports the rule that passing this point creates a second head. Crop-specific circuit wound gains remain uncited, and the 2021 solver still cannot be traced to numbered source equations. Panel D's hard-coded legend values and pulse shading also disagree with current simulation output despite the improved title." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
