        rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Morphometric validation: 48/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "This dimension has the clearest improvement. A one-parameter f2=1-a p model is fit to four octanol crop positions and evaluated, without refitting, against four innexin-RNAi positions; training RMSE is 4.2 points and held-out RMSE is 23.5 with r=0.94. The code reports these values in the figure and CSV, writes direct solver wavefronts, and measures anterior territory area on the photographic silhouette. This is a real model-data comparison rather than decorative anchors. It remains below the midpoint because four related positions are a very small validation set, no sampling uncertainty or baseline is reported, the 23.5-point held-out error is substantial, and the target is phenotype frequency while the predictor is a normalized signal-boundary index. The silhouette quantity is measured on a real body but is not compared with a measured treated specimen." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-measurement-anterior-body-area-fraction-on-s-mediterranea-silhouette-f2-1-f2-0-25>,
