    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — MorphoEval overall 55.6/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "A deterministic synthesis combines an explicitly labelled qualitative reaction–diffusion analogue, an orthogonal m3 profile, an educational rusty-matter circuit port, 14 curated PlanformDB records, a one-parameter crop-position fit and two fixed Planform cartoons. The additional outputs are cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png and cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv. The inert f3 and incorrect crop-wavefront defects are fixed, the silhouette is quantitatively sampled, and the empirical comparison now reports training and held-out errors. Remaining limits are the inaccessible full model papers, no f3-to-anatomy mapping, an uncited phenotype decision rule, weak held-out accuracy, fixed cartoon outcomes, illustrative time mapping and an incorrect reported f2 threshold caused by clipping in its inverse. Overall 55.6/100 (faithfulness 46.4, reproducibility 76.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a0d6848; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scipy 1.16.3, scikit-image 0.26.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 45, Morphological realism / specimen match 42, Parameter expressivity 58, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted). Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc; artifact_sha256: 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/planform/planform_canonical_silhouettes_v1.json=cac26e64a315ed81...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-17-cervera-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) model intercellular gap-junction blockade via effective diffusion reduction across AP (f2) and ML (f3) morphogen signals | Oviedo et al. (2010) and Durant et al. (2019) report crop-position-dependent double-head frequencies under octanol and triple-innexin RNAi and permanent two-headed regeneration after transient bioelectric depolarization; reconstructed_in_script: 1D AP (m1, m2) and ML (m3) reaction-diffusion analogue coupled with a 5-node bistable V_mem circuit port from MesmerPrism/rusty-matter and PlanformDB 2.5.0 canonical silhouettes; transfer_boundary: One-parameter octanol crop-gradient calibration transferred to held-out triple-innexin RNAi crop frequencies; does_not_claim: Exact equation-by-equation identity with the paywalled Cervera et al. (2021) full text or continuous 2D/3D biomechanical tissue deformation." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Calibrate or remove the illustrative 24-hour circuit overlay, generate legend values and pulse bounds from the simulation, and either source or remove the crop-specific rusty-matter wound-gain lookup.",
            "remediation needed: Fix f2_for_shift so it solves wavefront_for_f2(f2) = x_star_b without a clipped objective, test the recovered crossing, and correct the CSV/panel value from 0.20 to the actual approximately 0.42.",
            "remediation needed: Map f3 to a measured lateral morphology such as auricle width or head shape and compare it with specimens or source figures; otherwise describe f3 only as signal-profile expressivity.",
            "remediation needed: Obtain the full 2021 paper and map the analogue against its actual equations, boundary conditions, blocker factors and parameter definitions; retain the analogue label for every unmatched element.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the pharynx-crossing decision rule with a cited or empirically tested morphogen-to-phenotype mapping; if retaining this geometry, use actual body-mask bounds and state explicitly that the rule itself is an assumption.",
            "remediation needed: Validate the crop model on more independent experiments, include sampling uncertainty and simple baselines, and explain whether a 23.5-point held-out RMSE is adequate for the intended claim." ;
        pk:hasScore 5.56e-01 ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Parameter expressivity: 58/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Both named reaction–diffusion factors now have visible monotonic effects across stated sweeps: decreasing f2 advances x* and the silhouette's anterior area share, while decreasing f3 sharply lowers the ML centre/edge concentration ratio. The self-test asserts both monotonic f2 response and a non-inert f3 range, and panel E shows the profiles rather than a misleading 2D surface. Credit is limited because f3 changes only an independently normalized concentration curve and is never translated into lateral head or auricle form; morphology remains a binary cartoon switch. The circuit's crop-specific wound gains also remain a fixed lookup rather than an independently tested parameterization." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity-5> ;
        pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Reproducibility package: 84/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The environment exactly matched the recorded Python and five package versions, dependencies are locked, inputs are hash checked, and two complete runs produced byte-identical PNG, CSV and 46-frame GIF. The expanded self-test checks symmetry, f2 monotonicity, f3 sensitivity and every crop CSV wavefront, while port parity now compares all 11 frames and four state fields for every scenario and accurately says this is not biological validation. The package is held below a higher score because the test only checks that the fit metrics are finite, not correct; it misses the f2 inverse defect that prints 0.20 instead of the approximately 0.42 crossing; and it does not verify stale panel-D labels. The full prescribed repeat also took about 12.5 minutes, mostly because self-test renders the complete analysis figure." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package-2>,
