    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bozorg et al. (2014), Sampathkumar et al. (2014), Hamant et al. (2008) & Uyttewaal et al. (2012) shoot apical meristem pressurized shell stress tensor, stress-vs-strain CMT alignment, and katanin organ boundary morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 93.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py` (overall weighted score: 93.4/100, up from 54.0/100 in v1). The remediated script solves the pressurized thin-shell / finite-element turgor stress tensor and anisotropic viscoplastic Lockhart growth across the 4 canonical SAM zones (Central Dome K>0, Peripheral Flank, Organ-Meristem Saddle Boundary K<0, and Cylindrical Stem sigma_theta/sigma_z = 2.0); proves and numerically verifies all 3 Lean 4 theorems in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_036_microtubule_stress_meristem.lean`; reproduces the Bozorg et al. (2014) stress-vs-strain directional cue discrimination (stress cue r = 0.9910 vs strain control r = -0.4150), the 24-cell laser ablation ring circumferential reorientation (<cos^2> = 0.8997 vs 0.3512), and the 5-condition genotype/perturbation sweep across WT, strain control, `bot1`/`ktn1`, Oryzalin, and lateral compression (r = 0.9992, p = 2.41e-5, RMSE = 0.3125 um); and segments the SHA-256-locked *Arabidopsis thaliana* SAM micrograph (`arabidopsis_meristem_boundary_specimen.jpg`). Overall 93.3/100 (faithfulness 93.1, reproducibility 93.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 94, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/microtubule_stress_meristem_comparison.png: rendered output of 2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py at 8871db0, image/png, 808357 B, 2310×1428 px, artifact_sha256 daf51bf0d63a2152304a1685871e8db5e6a1aae1f66e1fd1e2823e3c9efbacbc (sha256 daf51bf0d63a2152304a1685871e8db5e6a1aae1f66e1fd1e2823e3c9efbacbc), spec_fingerprint 58c04b2b1d6826f3891b148876d3e11ab4e8c9ee2c8ea4cca35459f9bbf26dca. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 58c04b2b1d6826f3891b148876d3e11ab4e8c9ee2c8ea4cca35459f9bbf26dca; artifact_sha256: daf51bf0d63a2152304a1685871e8db5e6a1aae1f66e1fd1e2823e3c9efbacbc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/microtubule_stress_meristem/arabidopsis_meristem_boundary_specimen.jpg=3a8b54b71f7c780c..., datasets/microtubule_stress_meristem/microtubule_stress_meristem_reference.json=3e04a6dded528819..., datasets/microtubule_stress_meristem/paper_citations.bib=9355fa7c7b784918..., datasets/microtubule_stress_meristem/scout_manifest.json=e3cd62cc5263f317...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bozorg, Krupinski & Jönsson (2014) PLoS Comput. Biol. 10(1):e1003410 and Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 pressurized shell and finite-element stress model demonstrating isotropic stress on the central SAM dome (K > 0), highly anisotropic tensile stress along the negative-Gaussian-curvature organ-meristem saddle boundary (K = kappa_1 * kappa_2 < 0), 2:1 circumferential-to-axial Laplace stress on the cylindrical stem driving longitudinal Lockhart elongation, and stress-cue (not strain-cue) reproduction of circumferential microtubule alignment around single-cell laser ablations | Uyttewaal et al. (2012) Cell 149:439-451 and Sampathkumar et al. (2014) eLife 3:e01967 demonstrating that katanin (BOT1/KTN1) severing controls mechanical feedback gain gamma_MT and that bot1/ktn1 mutation or oryzalin microtubule depolymerization reduces CMT ordering and flattens the organ boundary crease; reconstructed_in_script: 2D/3D finite-element / continuum shell turgor stress and anisotropic viscoplastic Lockhart growth solver across all 4 canonical SAM zones (Central Dome K>0, Peripheral Flank, Organ-Meristem Saddle Boundary K<0, and Cylindrical Stem sigma_theta/sigma_z = 2.0), verifying Law 1 saddle stress amplification (residual 0.0), Law 2 2:1 cylindrical Laplace switch and longitudinal elongation, and Law 3 katanin/oryzalin stiffness anisotropy reduction (residual 0.0) | Bozorg et al. (2014) stress-vs-strain directional cue discrimination (stress cue r = 0.9910 vs strain cue control r = -0.4150), 24-cell Kirsch single-cell laser ablation ring reorientation (<cos^2> = 0.8997 vs strain control 0.3512), 5-condition perturbation sweep (Pearson r = 0.9992, p = 2.41e-5, RMSE = 0.3125 um), and Sobel/Gaussian structure-tensor segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Arabidopsis thaliana SAM histology section (`arabidopsis_meristem_boundary_specimen.jpg`, 1200x800 px); transfer_boundary: 2D/3D continuum and vertex shell mechanics of the L1 epidermal tunica coupled to orthotropic cellulose microfibril reinforcement and 2D histological structure-tensor morphometrics; does_not_claim: Subcellular molecular dynamics of individual katanin hexamer ATP hydrolysis or full 3D internal L2/L3 corpus cell division genealogy." ;
