    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Honda (1971) J. Theor. Biol. & Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 3D recursive dichotomous tree branching, effective leaf area optimization, and Leonardo da Vinci pipe-model cross-sectional area conservation — MorphoEval overall 94.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py` (overall weighted score: 94.1/100, up from 53.6/100 in v1). The remediated script implements Honda's (1971) full 3D local rotation-matrix tree builder across 4 crown archetypes over 6 branching orders (127 internodes, 64 terminal tips), verifies Leonardo da Vinci / Shinozaki pipe-model cross-sectional area conservation (ratio = 1.0000, RMSE = 0.00e+00 across 63 bifurcations), computes the Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 2D (theta_1, theta_2) effective leaf area optimization surface across 5-branch horizontal pagoda whorls (Pearson r = 0.99782, RMSE = 0.0128, p = 2.75e-8; Terminalia catappa optimum = 0.7739, Cornus controversa = 0.7591 vs 0.2001 in the collinear theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 ablation control), and segments the Pagoda Dogwood (Cornus controversa 'Variegata') specimen (`cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg`) to extract 7 horizontal pagoda tiers, theta_1 = 22.40 +- 8.18 deg, theta_2 = 50.93 +- 14.23 deg, and Leonardo area ratio beta = 0.9533 +- 0.1705 across N = 25 Y-bifurcations. Overall 94.0/100 (faithfulness 93.8, reproducibility 94.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 95, Morphological realism / specimen match 93, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 94, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 95, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/dichotomous_tree_branching_comparison.png: rendered output of 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py at 8871db0, image/png, 2148088 B, 2475×1575 px, artifact_sha256 581f4f616734e5fca1c57a025888323716a41e79137972f0611843524777aceb (sha256 581f4f616734e5fca1c57a025888323716a41e79137972f0611843524777aceb), spec_fingerprint eda105b6a09bddde8549d14c48bd6a5e37008bf9238b3585daf3bc48336da26b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eda105b6a09bddde8549d14c48bd6a5e37008bf9238b3585daf3bc48336da26b; artifact_sha256: 581f4f616734e5fca1c57a025888323716a41e79137972f0611843524777aceb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg=47cbd7225997789e..., datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/dichotomous_tree_branching_reference.json=9b8cd89b9fa19fbf...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-dichotomous-tree-branching-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Honda (1971) J. Theor. Biol. 31(2):331-338 3D recursive vector-rotation tree architecture parameterized by daughter divergence angles (theta_1, theta_2), length contraction ratios (r_1, r_2), and vertical phyllotactic roll angle alpha = 137.5 deg in the local horizontal plane spanned by v and v x z_hat | Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 199(4331):888-890 & Fisher & Honda (1979) Am. J. Bot. 66:633-644 demonstration that empirical branching angles (theta_1 approx 24-32 deg, theta_2 approx 52-62 deg) and contraction ratios (r_1 = 0.90, r_2 = 0.70) in Terminalia catappa and Cornus controversa maximize non-overlapping effective leaf area A_eff / A_total across 5-branch horizontal whorls | Shinozaki et al. (1964) Jpn. J. Ecol. 14:97-105 pipe-model theory and Eloy (2011) Phys. Rev. Lett. 107:258101 wind-stress derivation of Leonardo da Vinci's cross-sectional area conservation d_parent^Delta = d_1^Delta + d_2^Delta (Delta = 2.0); reconstructed_in_script: Full Honda (1971) 3D rotation-matrix tree builder (`grow_honda_1971_3d_tree`) across 4 botanical crown archetypes (excurrent conifer H/W = 1.12, pagoda tiered Cornus H/W = 0.45, decurrent deliquescent Quercus H/W = 0.44, and weeping pendulous Salix H/W = 0.53) over k = 6 orders (127 internodes, 64 terminal leaf clusters) | Honda & Fisher (1978) 5-whorl horizontal tier disk-union integration (`compute_effective_leaf_area_ratio`) and 2D (theta_1, theta_2) optimization surface (`evaluate_honda_fisher_optimization_surface`), matching the 8-regime benchmark curve (Pearson r = 0.99782, RMSE = 0.0128, p = 2.75e-8) and confirming Terminalia (0.7739) and Cornus (0.7591) outperform the collinear theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 ablation control (0.2001, a 74.14% self-shading penalty) | Exact Leonardo da Vinci / Shinozaki pipe-model sapwood area conservation (sum d_{k,i}^2 / d_0^2 = 1.0000 across all 6 orders and 63 bifurcations, RMSE = 0.00e+00) contrasted against Murray's vascular cube law (Delta = 3.0) and untapered cylinder controls | Computer-vision segmentation of the Pagoda Dogwood (Cornus controversa 'Variegata') specimen (`cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg`, Botanic Garden Meise, 960x1280 px) detecting 7 horizontal pagoda foliage tiers, 12,213 woody skeleton pixels, and 25 Y-bifurcations with empirical theta_1 = 22.40 +- 8.18 deg, theta_2 = 50.93 +- 14.23 deg, and Leonardo area ratio (d_1^2 + d_2^2)/d_0^2 = 0.9533 +- 0.1705; transfer_boundary: 3D recursive vector-rotation internode skeletons and 2D horizontal whorl leaf-cluster disk unions mapped to optical crown stratigraphy and woody bifurcation geometry of Cornus controversa; does_not_claim: Cambial auxin-cytokinin molecular transport kinetics or turbulent eddy-resolvable wind-tunnel aeroelasticity at individual leaf blades." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple 3D Honda tiered crowns to solar-elevation radiative transfer ray-tracing across diurnal sun paths to compare equatorial vs temperate latitude optimal tier spacing." ;
        pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

