        dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py` (overall weighted score: 93.8/100, up from 53.0/100 in v1). The remediated script solves the coupled M = 16 multicellular Bentley-Gerhardt-Bates VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 ODE network and 2D filopodial angiogenic sprout elongation across all 5 canonical regimes — Physiological VEGF salt-and-pepper (tip fraction = 0.5000, Brillouin I_pi = 0.9472), High uniform VEGF oscillations (temporal CV = 0.3808, rescued by soluble Flt1 decoy to I_pi = 0.9480), DAPT Notch blockade all-tip hypersprouting (tip fraction = 1.0000, 0 stalk cells), Dll4+/- haploinsufficiency (tip fraction = 0.7500), and WT : Vegfr2+/- mosaic competition (WT tip occupancy = 0.8571); reproduces the 8-point Notch gain sweep (Pearson r = 0.99781, RMSE = 0.0136, p = 2.61e-8); and segments the SHA-256-locked Homo sapiens HUVEC angiogenic sprouting vascular network micrograph (plexus density = 0.1967, 69 branch junctions, 58 sprouting tips, tip/junction ratio = 0.8406, inter-tip NND CV = 0.7003). Overall 93.8/100 (faithfulness 93.8, reproducibility 93.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 95, Morphological realism / specimen match 93, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 94, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/vascular_angiogenesis_notch_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py at 8871db0, image/png, 739170 B, 2490×1530 px, artifact_sha256 467bd8172c349e7c8b916ab51cfba991d573bc7cc2a730ed158284d46321247a (sha256 467bd8172c349e7c8b916ab51cfba991d573bc7cc2a730ed158284d46321247a), spec_fingerprint 75ad27375139b901d6c87702d5f02c739a8e698db79579ceae73bdab1d021c1b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 75ad27375139b901d6c87702d5f02c739a8e698db79579ceae73bdab1d021c1b; artifact_sha256: 467bd8172c349e7c8b916ab51cfba991d573bc7cc2a730ed158284d46321247a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/huvec_angiogenic_sprouting_plexus_specimen.jpg=9bf4f3e2692bd2ac..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/paper_citations.bib=a96e44f99de8a756..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/scout_manifest.json=2b97b38c418e4c44..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/vascular_angiogenesis_notch_reference.json=8821743569ceaf2e...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol. 4:e1000052 & Collier et al. (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 183:429-446 coupled endothelial VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 lateral-inhibition ODE network destabilizing via the Brillouin-zone k = pi antisymmetric mode into period-2 Tip-Stalk-Tip-Stalk salt-and-pepper alternation under physiological VEGF and synchronous oscillations under high uniform VEGF | Hellström et al. (2007) Nature 445:776-780 pharmacological gamma-secretase Notch blockade (DAPT, k_t -> 0 => N_i = 0 => V_i = V_max) producing 100% all-tip hypersprouting syncytial sheets and Dll4+/- haploinsufficiency producing ~75% tip hyperbranching | Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. 12:943-953 chimeric WT : Vegfr2+/- mosaic tip competition (~87.5% WT tip occupancy) and Chappell et al. (2009) Dev. Cell 17:377-386 soluble VEGFR1 (sFlt1) decoy sequestration rescuing salt-and-pepper patterning under VEGF overload; reconstructed_in_script: Coupled M = 16 endothelial cell VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 + 2D filopodial angiogenic sprout elongation solver (`simulate_vessel_notch_sprouting`) and Brillouin k = pi linear stability & sFlt1 decoy verifier (`verify_brillouin_instability_and_flt1_rescue`) | 5 canonical angiogenic regimes + sFlt1 rescue control (`evaluate_angiogenic_regimes`): Physiological salt-and-pepper (tip fraction = 0.5000, I_pi = 0.9472), High uniform VEGF oscillations (temporal CV = 0.3808, rescued by sFlt1 to CV = 0.0134 and I_pi = 0.9480), DAPT Notch blockade (tip fraction = 1.0000, 0 stalk cells, I_pi = 0.0000), Dll4+/- haploinsufficiency (tip fraction = 0.7500), and WT : Vegfr2+/- mosaic competition (WT tip share = 0.8571) | 8-point Notch trans-activation gain sweep across k_t in [0.00, 1.25] reproducing the Hellström et al. (2007) / Bentley et al. (2008) tip-cell fraction continuum (Pearson r = 0.99781, RMSE = 0.0136, p = 2.61e-8) and Brillouin k = pi alternation index (Pearson r = 0.99809, RMSE = 0.0227, p = 1.66e-8) | Computer-vision medial-axis skeleton segmentation of `huvec_angiogenic_sprouting_plexus_specimen.jpg` (CC BY 4.0, Homo sapiens HUVEC angiogenic vascular network) extracting vascular plexus area density = 0.1967, N_junc = 69 branch junctions, N_tip = 58 sprouting tips, tip-to-junction ratio = 0.8406, and inter-tip NND CV = 0.7003 (31.11 +- 21.79 px); transfer_boundary: 1D periodic M=16 endothelial vessel wall coupled to 2D filopodial sprout outgrowth and medial-axis topological skeletonization of calcein-stained HUVEC vascular networks; does_not_claim: 3D Navier-Stokes blood hemodynamics, pericyte PDGFRB recruitment, or shear-induced arteriovenous remodeling after lumen perfusion." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
