    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — MorphoEval overall 71.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Decodes the Limbform formalism (segments as graph edges with length and direction, joints as vertices with border radii, sub-joints for grafts, digits with phalanx counts) for 555 of the 565 morphology rows of LimbformDB 2.1.0 — the other 10 are outcome labels without geometry — and draws each limb as a smooth outline through the joint control points with the paper's proximodistal red-to-blue gradient, green coxa, yellow basis/trochanter, black long bones and blue digits. Against the paper's own cartoons of the five Fig. 1 wild types the decoded silhouettes have the same topology, pose and segment/digit counts; bounding-box-aligned IoU is 0.41-0.74 (best for the cricket leg, worst for the frog hindlimb, where the thigh-shank angle differs). The joint-radius rule of the formalism holds for 3137 of 3146 joints when a sub-joint counts its host segment twice. Overall 71.3/100 (faithfulness 70.0, reproducibility 74.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 747c57f; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 65, Parameter expressivity 75, Morphometric validation 55, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 65. Output judged: limbform_wildtype_gallery.png: rendered output of 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py at 747c57f, image/png, 620043 B, 2400×1875 px, artifact_sha256 d561f4aab10756976c3fd5caf7a8c516da13c1cd9395d6cb5a54b8a2f5b10236 (sha256 d561f4aab10756976c3fd5caf7a8c516da13c1cd9395d6cb5a54b8a2f5b10236)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Ask the Lobo lab for the LimbformDB licence so the file can be vendored with its hash.",
            "remediation needed: Compare at least the five wild types with photographs of the real limbs (Fig. 1 A-E), e.g. segment-length ratios, not only with the paper's cartoons.",
            "remediation needed: Confirm the Ang convention and the joint-radius order against the Limbform software source or the authors, and explain the Fig. 1 B''/C'' silhouette residuals.",
            "remediation needed: Pin the Python 3.14 environment (exact versions) in requirements or a lock file." ;
        pk:hasScore 7.13e-01 ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Parameter expressivity: 75/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Every encoded number has a visible effect: each radius moves one control point of the outline, each segment's Dist/Ang moves its distal joint and everything beyond it, each sub-joint places a graft, each digit's Dist/Ang/NumBones draws one digit. Morphologies in one frame share one scale, so size differences between phenotypes are preserved. There is no parameter sweep in the output and Side/Reversed/Inverted are only reported (no 2.1.0 entry uses them), so their effect is untested." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
