    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Morphological realism / specimen match: 65/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The only published renderings of these database entries are the cartoons in Fig. 1 of the Regeneration paper; side by side, the decoded axolotl forelimb, Xenopus hindlimb, fiddler-crab walking leg, cricket T3 leg and huntsman-spider leg have the same segments, digits, pose and colour scheme (gradient, coxa green, basis yellow, bones, digits). Measured on the figure, bounding-box-aligned silhouette IoU is 0.64, 0.41, 0.43, 0.74 and 0.49 for panels A''-E'': the cricket leg is essentially identical, the others differ in joint angles and segment width (the frog thigh-shank angle most of all), which may reflect a database revision after the figure was drawn or an angle convention not captured. Distinct morphologies (double limbs, grafts, branched chelipeds, missing segments) render distinctly. No photographs of real limbs are compared." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
