    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — MorphoEval overall 64.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "raup_shell(W, D, T, S) sweeps an ellipse of radial semi-axis a = a0 W^(theta/2pi) and axial semi-axis a/S, centred at r_c = a(1+D)/(1-D) from the axis and z_c = T r_c along it, in the plane through the axis. self_test() recovers W, D, T from meshes on a 3x3x4 grid to 4.9e-15 and checks the spire's axial travel rises strictly with T (the outer height/width may stay flat while the last whorl still envelops the spire, which is correct behaviour for involute forms); a T=0 shell is checked to be exactly one aperture thick. Six illustrative panels (W, D, T from variables.json) rendered rotating in side and overhead view; W x D and W x T sheets; a six-panel still with height/width; a CSV of nominal and recovered W, D, T per panel with height/width and spire/width. The measurements sidecar recovers W, D, T again, independently, from the script's generating function. Overall 64.1/100 (faithfulness 58.6, reproducibility 77.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit ba6fd20; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 45, Parameter expressivity 70, Morphometric validation 45, Source and data traceability 75, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 80. Output judged: raup_shell_animation.gif: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at ba6fd20, image/gif, 15189434 B, 1200×800 px, 100 frames, artifact_sha256 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02 (sha256 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02), spec_fingerprint 99d02b160418b61e3ca5605bf1327defebc58c14533242de5ba9809a805bf905. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 99d02b160418b61e3ca5605bf1327defebc58c14533242de5ba9809a805bf905; artifact_sha256: 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/raup/variables.json=c9c9cfaf70faa9a5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-13-morphology-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Raup (1966), Noshita (2014), and Okabe & Yoshimura (2017) define logarithmic helicospiral shell coiling via whorl expansion W, radial distance D = r_min/r_max, translation T = dz_c/dr_c, and aperture shape S; reconstructed_in_script: Parametric 3D surface generator raup_shell(W, D, T, S) with exact inverse parameter recovery recover_parameters() to < 1e-14 error across a 3x3x4 morphospace grid; transfer_boundary: Six illustrative parameter sets in datasets/raup/variables.json labelled cf. canonical shell forms (planispiral, turreted, evolute disc, obconical, high-spired, globose); does_not_claim: Direct morphometric measurement of physical museum shell specimens or micro-CT meshes." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Obtain Raup 1966 and pin the definitions of W, D, T, S to its equations and figures; confirm the direction of the S ratio.",
            "remediation needed: Put a real shell beside at least one panel - a photograph, or a specimen's measured (W, D, T) from Raup 1967's ammonoid table or a later gastropod dataset - and measure the agreement.",
            "remediation needed: Report the stored frame count after saving the GIF, or write it with a writer that does not merge frames.",
            "remediation needed: Sweep S and D on their own in the parameter sheet; mark Raup's block-diagram regions (gastropods, ammonoids, bivalves, brachiopods) on the W x T and W x D sheets once the paper is in hand." ;
        pk:hasScore 6.41e-01 ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
