    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — MorphoEval overall 70.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-16"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Downloads the WormGUIDES atlas at a pinned commit and verifies 429 files against a SHA-256 manifest; decodes the 360 StarryNite nuclei tables with the column semantics of the WormGUIDES loader (valid flag, x, y, z, diameter, lineage name) and the movie-start offset of ProductionInfo.csv; checks that all 1330 distinct names follow the Sulston grammar and that every cell whose parent is in the movie appears after it (1326/1326); re-derives the lineage chart from the names; sets the atlas's own eggshell outline mesh at frame 330 to the 50 um egg length (0.1649 um per unit; the shell's unfitted width comes out 29.2 um, the 13 sampled shell meshes bracket the scale at 0.1649-0.1750, the earlier nuclear-cloud estimate was 0.1617); draws the nuclei to scale inside the shell outline at six stages, 51 single-cell meshes at frame 330 and the c302 connectome adjacency matrix (300 neurons after name canonicalisation). Reports that the atlas reuses a static shell mesh for frames 1-~250 that the nuclei overrun by up to 19 units. Against WormAtlas's quotation of Sulston et al. the cell-stage anchors agree (113 listed deaths all present, 562-571 nuclei at 330-350 min against ~550, E-cell ingression at 26 cells against the ~30-cell stage) but the clock runs ~27 min ahead (gastrulation at movie-minute 73 against 100), which the script reports and does not resolve. Overall 70.2/100 (faithfulness 67.6, reproducibility 76.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 303a87e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 62, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 70. Output judged: celegans_four_views.png: rendered output of 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py at 303a87e, image/png, 424197 B, 2240×1680 px, artifact_sha256 eb4b60086280c9a1740358c26fc655598f25d2adad63a9fcdb9c3a7980cc3bd6 (sha256 eb4b60086280c9a1740358c26fc655598f25d2adad63a9fcdb9c3a7980cc3bd6). Supersedes audit: 2026-10-15-celegans-audit." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Draw the connectome with chemical and electrical edges separated, and keep the muscle/end-organ nodes that Cook et al. include.",
            "remediation needed: Pin the Python 3.14 environment (exact versions) in requirements or a lock file.",
            "remediation needed: Place a WormGUIDES figure panel (Santella et al. 2015 is CC BY) or a DIC frame beside the decoded nuclei at the same stage and measure the agreement.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the 50 um assumption with the acquisition voxel size of DISPIM_061416 (not in the repository's ProductionInfo.csv; ask the Bao lab), and ask why the shell mesh is static for frames 1-~250 while the nuclei overrun it.",
            "remediation needed: Resolve the ~27 min clock offset against Sulston's schedule (recording temperature, or the meaning of \"movie start time 20 min\") with the Bao lab or the diSPIM metadata." ;
        pk:hasScore 7.02e-01 ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

